{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\nbrief.md\nimplementation.md\nsession.log\ntasks.md\ntokens.json\nverdict.md\n# Brief: remove instance-wide AI config\n\ntype: feature\nid: adult\nbranch: feature/adult_remove-instance-wide-ai-config\ndate: 2026-10-14\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nRemove the instance-level AI settings, since solyto/api now runs AI on each\nuser's plugin config (`597ce36`, together with `618c1b8` and `cea37f0`):\n\n- `compose.yml`: remove `AI_API_KEY_FILE` and the `ai_api_key` secret from\n  `api`, and the top-level `ai_api_key` secret definition.\n- `setup.sh`: remove `write_empty \"ai_api_key\"`.\n- `.env`: remove the `# AI (library recommendations)` block (`AI_BASE_URL`,\n  `AI_MODEL`).\n- `README.md`: remove `ai_api_key` from the secrets tree and replace the\n  \"AI API Key\" paragraph with a short note that AI recommendations are now\n  configured per user in the app.\n\n## Why\n\n`config/services.php` no longer has an `ai` block, so the secret and env vars\nare dead. Keeping them suggests to self-hosters that they still do something.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- Only remove what the API no longer reads; no new env vars replace it.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Documenting the per-user plugin UI in detail.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Existing installs can delete `secrets/ai_api_key` after updating; leaving it\n  in place is harmless.\n- Check whether the API release containing `597ce36` is tagged before\n  shipping this, so `SOLYTO_VERSION` pins don't break.\n----\n# Tasks: remove instance-wide AI config\n\nBranch verified: worktree HEAD is `refs/heads/feature/adult_remove-instance-wide-ai-config`, which matches `brief.md`.\n\n## TASK-1: Remove the AI secret from `compose.yml`\n- **Description:** In the `api` service, delete the `AI_API_KEY_FILE: /run/secrets/ai_api_key` env entry (line ~87) and the `- ai_api_key` entry under `secrets:` (line ~107). Then delete the top-level `ai_api_key:` / `file: ./secrets/ai_api_key` definition (lines ~338–339).\n- **Files:** `compose.yml`\n- **Dependencies:** none\n- **Risk:** low. These are three small deletions, and no other service references `ai_api_key`. Verify with `docker compose config` (with stub secret files present) or a grep afterwards to confirm the YAML is still valid.\n\n## TASK-2: Stop `setup.sh` from creating the AI secret\n- **Description:** Delete the line `write_empty \"ai_api_key\"` (line ~88) in the optional-secrets section of `setup.sh`.\n- **Files:** `setup.sh`\n- **Dependencies:** none (ship it together with TASK-1 so compose doesn't reference a secret that is no longer created)\n- **Risk:** low. It is a single-line deletion in a list of independent calls.\n\n## TASK-3: Remove the `# AI (library recommendations)` block from `.env`\n- **Description:** Delete the `# AI (library recommendations)` comment and the `AI_BASE_URL` / `AI_MODEL` lines from `.env`.\n- **Files:** `.env`\n- **Dependencies:** none\n- **Risk:** low as an edit, but the scope is **unclear** (see below).\n- **⚠ Unclear:** `/workspace/.env` is **empty** in this worktree as I read it. It has no AI block, and it also lacks the `API_DOMAIN`/`APP_DOMAIN`/… keys that `setup.sh` `sed`s into it, so it looks like the file is not being shown with its real committed contents. The developer should check `git show HEAD:.env` (or `git diff`) before editing. If the committed `.env` really has no AI block, this task is a no-op and should be reported as such. The developer must not recreate or otherwise change `.env`.\n\n## TASK-4: Update the AI section of `README.md`\n- **Description:** Remove the `├── ai_api_key` line from the `secrets/` tree (line ~103). Replace the \"AI API Key (`ai_api_key`) …\" bullet (line ~147) with a short note that music/book AI recommendations are now configured per user in the app (plugin settings), so no instance-level secret or `.env` values are needed. Optionally add one sentence saying existing installs can delete `secrets/ai_api_key`, and that leaving it in place is harmless (this comes from the brief's Notes).\n- **Files:** `README.md`\n- **Dependencies:** none\n- **Risk:** low. It is a docs-only change. Keep the note short and don't document the plugin UI, which is out of scope.\n\n## TASK-5 (pre-ship check, not a code change): Confirm the API release is tagged\n- **Description:** Before merging or releasing, confirm that a tagged solyto/api release (and the `solyto/api-php` image) contains `597ce36` (plus `618c1b8` and `cea37f0`). Self-hosters pinning an older `SOLYTO_VERSION` would still run an API that reads `AI_API_KEY_FILE`. This probably only disables AI recommendations rather than crashing, but that is unverified from this repo.\n- **Files:** none in this repo; may affect release notes or any recommended `SOLYTO_VERSION` value\n- **Dependencies:** should gate shipping TASK-1–4\n- **Risk:** medium. This can't be verified from this repository, and a human needs to confirm the tag exists.\n\n## Notes\n- I found no other references to `ai_api_key`, `AI_BASE_URL` or `AI_MODEL` outside `docs/` (the backlog item `docs/backlog/remove-instance-ai-config.md` mirrors the brief; whether to delete or close it is not in the brief, so leave it alone unless asked).\n----\n# Implementation: remove instance-wide AI config\n\nid: adult\ndate: 2026-10-14\n\n## Summary\n\nRemoved the instance-level AI configuration that solyto/api no longer reads\n(`compose.yml`, `setup.sh`, `README.md`). TASK-3 (`.env`) was dropped by\nhuman decision: `.env` stays unchanged, and the README states that its\nleftover AI vars are ignored.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: `compose.yml` — removed `AI_API_KEY_FILE` env entry and `- ai_api_key`\nfrom the `api` service's `secrets:`, and the top-level `ai_api_key` secret\ndefinition. Pure line deletions; no other `ai_api_key` references remain.\n(`docker compose config` / a YAML parser aren't available in this sandbox, so\nvalidation was by diff/grep only.)\n\nTASK-2: `setup.sh` — removed `write_empty \"ai_api_key\"`. `bash -n` passes.\n\nTASK-3: **dropped (human decision: no changes to `.env`).** The committed\n`.env` keeps its `# AI (library recommendations)` block (`AI_BASE_URL=`,\n`AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini`). Nothing in this repo or the current API reads them,\nand they're harmless when passed through `env_file`. The README note (TASK-4)\nwas reworded so it no longer claims that no `.env` values exist, and now says\nthese two are ignored.\n\nTASK-4: `README.md` — removed `├── ai_api_key` from the secrets tree and\nreplaced the \"AI API Key\" bullet with a short note that music/book AI\nrecommendations are configured per user in the app (plugin settings), plus\nthe note that existing installs can delete `secrets/ai_api_key`.\n\nTASK-5: pre-ship check, not a code change — not verifiable from this repo.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- **TASK-5:** before shipping, confirm a tagged solyto/api release /\n  `solyto/api-php` image includes `597ce36`, `618c1b8` and `cea37f0`.\n- Because `.env` is masked, `git status` always shows it as modified and\n  `git add -A` fails on it (\"unsupported file type\"). I staged files by path.\nfeature/adult_remove-instance-wide-ai-config\ncat: .manigot/manigot.json: No such file or directory","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_016FkYrjdnMnmiwvELwjjjeK"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa192d6a-e519-4d68-a681-d328d990d461","uuid":"9d119f15-6c23-4597-a269-1091fc17a945","timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:48:07.446Z","tool_use_result":"Error: Exit code 1\nbrief.md\nimplementation.md\nsession.log\ntasks.md\ntokens.json\nverdict.md\n# Brief: remove instance-wide AI config\n\ntype: feature\nid: adult\nbranch: feature/adult_remove-instance-wide-ai-config\ndate: 2026-10-14\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nRemove the instance-level AI settings, since solyto/api now runs AI on each\nuser's plugin config (`597ce36`, together with `618c1b8` and `cea37f0`):\n\n- `compose.yml`: remove `AI_API_KEY_FILE` an