es in compose.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `setup.sh` removes `write_empty \"ai_api_key\"`, and `bash -n setup.sh` passes.\n\nTASK-3: FAIL\nnotes: Not done (implementation.md says so openly, because `.env` is masked in the sandbox). `git show HEAD:.env` lines 68–72 still contain\n`# AI (library recommendations)`, the two comment lines, `AI_BASE_URL=` and `AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini`. The brief explicitly requires removing this block. As a result, the new README note (\"no instance-level secret or `.env` values are needed\") is currently contradicted by the shipped `.env`.\n\nTASK-4: PASS\nnotes: `README.md` removes `├── ai_api_key` from the secrets tree and replaces the \"AI API Key\" bullet with a short per-user note, including the \"existing installs can delete `secrets/ai_api_key`; leaving it in place is harmless\" note. It doesn't go into plugin UI detail, so it stays in scope.\n\nTASK-5: NOT VERIFIABLE (pre-ship check, no code)\nnotes: This repo can't confirm that a tagged solyto/api release / `solyto/api-php` image contains `597ce36`, `618c1b8` and `cea37f0`. A human must confirm this before shipping (the brief's Notes).\n\n## Security\n\nNot run. This change only removes config.\n\n## Overall\n\nNEEDS WORK\n\nMust change before merge:\n1. Remove the `# AI (library recommendations)` block (comment lines plus `AI_BASE_URL=` and `AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini`, and the surrounding extra blank line) from the committed `.env` on this branch. This has to be done by someone with real access to `.env`, since the agent sandbox masks it.\n2. Before shipping, confirm that the solyto/api release containing `597ce36` (+ `618c1b8`, `cea37f0`) is tagged and published as `solyto/api-php`, so `SOLYTO_VERSION` pins don't break.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Q5LzPokbWUAUTz5YaBiUAj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
